{"chunk_id": "1a461c8db6d7", "text": "Arjuna declares ominous signs before the coming war: his weapons tremble to be used, wild creatures follow his chariot, and celestial portents foretell slaughter. Confident in the divine weapons he has received\u2014Pasupata, Brahma, and others\u2014he vows that if battle begins the sons of Dhritarashtra will not survive. The narrative then shifts to Bhishma addressing Duryodhana. Bhishma recounts an ancient tale in which the divine sages Nara and Narayana aided the gods against the Asuras. He reveals that these same primordial beings are now incarnate as Arjuna (Nara) and Krishna (Narayana), united for a world\u2011shaping conflict and effectively invincible. Bhishma warns Duryodhana that ignoring this truth will doom the Kauravas. Karna responds defensively, insisting on his loyalty to Duryodhana and rejecting Bhishma\u2019s criticism, further exposing the hardened divisions leading to war.\nBhishma warns Duryodhana that Krishna and Arjuna are the divine pair Nara and Narayana, recounting their ancient deeds and foretelling Kaurava destruction.\nThemes: divine incarnation, prophecy of defeat, cosmic mythology, loyalty and defiance", "vector": [0.0005181634332984686, -0.01574486680328846, -0.01440403051674366, 0.021586131304502487, -0.004357716999948025, 0.015094361267983913, -0.025170544162392616, 0.007016156800091267, -0.013043280690908432, -0.012883973307907581, 0.013514564372599125, 0.00833044108003378, -0.01099220011383295, 0.007414424791932106, 0.0012055907864123583, 0.009618175216019154, 0.050208333879709244, -0.010142561048269272, 0.03236592188477516, -0.021745439618825912, -0.009784120135009289, -0.0018154388526454568, 0.008741985075175762, 0.01696622185409069, -0.012445878237485886, 0.02221008576452732, 0.011350641027092934, -0.028622202575206757, 0.0035777753219008446, -0.024068670347332954, -0.013408360071480274, -0.0026119749527424574, 0.012923800386488438, -0.004706201609224081, -0.026936199516057968, 0.0066942232